---
// Who built this, on every route (#544).
//
// RENDERED BY THE LAYOUT, NOT BY EACH PAGE. Every route goes through
// Base.astro, so a new page gets the credit without anyone remembering it, and
// `npm run smoke` reads every built page for it and checks one page of every
// route in a browser — which is what catches a page that stops using Base.
//
// STATIC: TWO LINKS AND NO ISLAND. This sits on `/`, which perf-budget.json
// holds at zero JavaScript, so anything here that needed hydrating would cost
// the landing page the React floor.
//
// The name is the way in to /about; nothing else on the site links there. The
// GitHub link is the profile, the same one README.md's credit line carries —
// /about is where the repository itself is linked.
//
// Quiet links, in the register of the landing page's own — dust, turning
// starlight with a violet underline on hover — because this line sits under
// the one glowing field on `/` and must not read as a second invitation. The
// underline is dust rather than the landing page's `line`: the links are the
// same colour as "Built by", so the underline is the only thing marking them as
// links (WCAG 1.4.1), and `line` on `void` is 1.4:1 — there, but barely seen.
// Each link is a 24px box for WCAG 2.2 AA 2.5.8, the size the tap-target sweep
// in `npm run smoke` measures.
const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/opendroid';
const LINK =
  'inline-flex min-h-[24px] items-center text-dust underline decoration-dust underline-offset-4 hover:text-starlight hover:decoration-thread';
---

<footer class="border-t border-line px-[26px] py-3.5 text-[13px] text-dust">
  {/*
    The space expressions are load-bearing (#480): Astro trims the newline
    between text and an anchor rather than collapsing it to a space.
  */}
  Built by <a href="/about" class={LINK}>Ajay Thakur</a> &middot;{' '}
  <a href={GITHUB} class={LINK}>GitHub</a>
</footer>
